{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Transmission Control Protocol.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Transmission Control Protocol.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"transmission control protocol transmission control protocol","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Transmission Control Protocol.md","fileName":"Transmission Control Protocol.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Transmission Control Protocol","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 21:06\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Internet Infrastructure History]] [[TCP UDP and Internet Protocol Addressing]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Internet Infrastructure History","TCP UDP and Internet Protocol Addressing","User Datagram Protocol","computing.epub","gameprogrammingalgorithmsandtechniques.pdf","hands-onnetworkprogrammingwithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Transmission Control Protocol.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Transmission Control Protocol.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"transmission control protocol transmission control protocol","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Transmission Control Protocol.md","fileName":"Transmission Control Protocol.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Transmission Control Protocol","heading":"Transmission Control Protocol","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Transmission Control Protocol provides a reliable ordered data stream over an unreliable packet network. It divides application data, tracks delivery, retransmits missing pieces, and reassembles the original sequence.\n\nTCP operates end to end between hosts rather than requiring every network link to guarantee delivery. Applications can use its service without managing each packet directly.\n\nThis reliability can add delay when a missing segment blocks later data until retransmission succeeds. Games therefore use TCP for information that must arrive intact, while rapidly changing real-time updates often favor [[User Datagram Protocol]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Internet Infrastructure History","TCP UDP and Internet Protocol Addressing","User Datagram Protocol","computing.epub","gameprogrammingalgorithmsandtechniques.pdf","hands-onnetworkprogrammingwithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Transmission Control Protocol.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Transmission Control Protocol.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"transmission control protocol transmission control protocol","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Transmission Control Protocol.md","fileName":"Transmission Control Protocol.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Transmission Control Protocol","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[computing.epub]]\n[[gameprogrammingalgorithmsandtechniques.pdf]]\n\n[[hands-onnetworkprogrammingwithcandnetcore.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Internet Infrastructure History","TCP UDP and Internet Protocol Addressing","User Datagram Protocol","computing.epub","gameprogrammingalgorithmsandtechniques.pdf","hands-onnetworkprogrammingwithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}